New profiles open dark, with the Grabzy.CC green as the colour seed, so the
browser matches the website: near-black surfaces, green for what is active.
Settings > Appearance can still change both; incognito stays grayscale.

The hunks carry no context on purpose. Chromium 158 dropped the deprecated
prefs that sat around these two lines, so no context fits both 157 and 158;
each replaced line appears once in theme_service.cc (156 through 158).

--- a/chrome/browser/themes/theme_service.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/themes/theme_service.cc
@@ -324 +324 @@
-      std::to_underlying(ThemeService::BrowserColorScheme::kSystem));
+      std::to_underlying(ThemeService::BrowserColorScheme::kDark));
@@ -325 +325,3 @@
-  registry->RegisterIntegerPref(prefs::kUserColor, SK_ColorTRANSPARENT);
+  // Grabzy.CC: the website's live green seeds the Material palette.
+  registry->RegisterIntegerPref(prefs::kUserColor,
+                                SkColorSetRGB(0x2E, 0xE8, 0x7A));
